    "correctAnswer": "D",
    "correctLetterFull": "D",
    "correctOptionIndex": 3,
    "explanation": "Carrie used the analogous estimating technique, which is a form of expert judgment. It is a tool and technique of the Estimate Activity Durations process. Analogous estimating bases estimates on previous activities that are similar in fact, and they require the person estimating them to have expertise in the activity. Analogous estimating techniques are typically used to estimate project duration when there is a limited amount of information about the project.",
