    "explanation": "A highly predictive (waterfall) life cycle typically has detailed specifications, with requirements defined up front before work begins. A highly adaptive life cycle (Agile) has requirements that are progressively elaborated on, and delivery occurs frequently. Change within a predictive life cycle is constrained, while adaptive encourages change to be incorporated in real time during delivery.",
