    "chapterNumber": 6,
    "chapter": "Chapter 6: Full-Length Practice Exam 3",
    "originalNumber": 188,
    "question": "A project manager of a construction company uncovered a risk that, if it were to occur, could shorten the length of the project by two months. This would mean a savings of $75,000 for the company. All of the stakeholders agreed that anything within reason should be done to make sure that this risk happens. What risk response strategy is the project manager most likely to use?",
